    "q-107931": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107931",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A sphere has a surface area of $48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Calculate the diameter of the sphere.",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 48\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{48\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
