      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The surface area of a sphere is $144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Find the volume of the sphere.",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the above formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 144\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{144\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =36 \\\\ r & =6\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we  can find the volume of the sphere as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (6)^{3} \\\\  & =288\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
